# One rule instead of a list: no canonical URL on this site ends in a slash
# (trailingSlash:'never'), so any request that does is wrong by definition.
#
# This exists because html_handling:'drop-trailing-slash' only redirects when an
# asset actually exists at the slash-less path. Redirect-only routes have no HTML
# file, so /models/ fell through to the 404 page instead of reaching the
# /models -> /blueprints rule. This catches those before the Worker's asset
# handling runs, and issues a 301 rather than html_handling's uncacheable 307.
#
# The Cloudflare adapter APPENDS its generated rules below this line, so
# everything here is matched first. Keep it that way.
/*/    /:splat    301
